          "text": "Internally widen the upper bound to max(alpha,beta) only when invoking the existing score-square producer. Its actual probability and gradient norm-square L1 give vector MemLp2 and Bochner L1. The shared theorem has no alpha<=beta premise; the dimension-zero case is retained.",
          "formula": "\\bar\\beta=\\max(\\alpha,\\beta),\\quad\\mu\\propto e^{-U}dx,\\quad\\nabla U\\in L^2(\\mu)\\subset L^1(\\mu).",
          "lean": "GibbsGradientMoment.gibbs_gradient_moment; memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm; MemLp.integrable"
