          "title": "Recover ordinary full-space weighted integrability",
          "text": "The canonical curvature-to-strong-convexity and Gibbs integrability providers yield integrable exp(-U) against ordinary volume. The actual tilted-law equivalence converts gradient L1 into exp(-U) times gradient L1 against this same volume. Its directional inner product is integrable for every v.",
          "formula": "w=e^{-U},\\quad w\\in L^1(dx),\\quad w\\nabla U\\in L^1(dx),\\quad w\\langle\\nabla U,v\\rangle\\in L^1(dx).",
          "lean": "QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic; StrongConvexGibbsIntegrability.integrable_exp_neg_of_strongConvexOn; integrable_tilted_iff; Integrable.inner_const"
        },
